{"paper": "SSC-DelhiPoliceConstable-01-Dec-2023-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 15, "tagged_count": 15, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "In five subjects of equal marks, S gets 45, 78, 36, 65 and 56 in the first semester and 48, 72, 55, 46 and 79 in the second semester. What are his average marks in the first year?", "options": [{"text": "57", "added": false}, {"text": "56", "added": false}, {"text": "58", "added": false}, {"text": "58.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "A garrison of 1500 men has provisions for 11 days. How long will the provisions last if the garrison is increased by 1800 men?", "options": [{"text": "3 days", "added": false}, {"text": "6 days", "added": false}, {"text": "5 days", "added": false}, {"text": "4 days", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "group-work", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "Shanti while driving her car at a speed of 68 km/h, observes that at some moment a moving bus is 40 m ahead of her car. After 10 sec she finds that she is 60 m ahead of the bus. What is the speed of the bus?", "options": [{"text": "30 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "32 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "25 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "38 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "relative-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "A person promised to pay ₹9,048 to the bank in 5 equal annual instalments at the rate of 8% per annum simple interest. The annual instalment (in ₹) paid is:", "options": [{"text": "1560", "added": false}, {"text": "1050", "added": false}, {"text": "1650", "added": false}, {"text": "1100", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-instalments", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "The average age of three persons is 54 years and their ages are in the proportion 2 : 3 : 4. Find the age of the youngest person.", "options": [{"text": "28 years", "added": false}, {"text": "34 years", "added": false}, {"text": "36 years", "added": false}, {"text": "32 years", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ages", "sub": "ratio-of-ages", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "15028.71", "added": false}, {"text": "15258.71", "added": false}, {"text": "15528.71", "added": false}, {"text": "13404.76", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "compounding-frequency", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "The greatest number that exactly divides 126, 198 and 162 is:", "options": [{"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "27", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}, {"text": "81", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "Pihu buys a chocolate for ₹225 and sells it for ₹300. What will be her gain percentage? (Rounded off to two decimal places)", "options": [{"text": "33.33%", "added": false}, {"text": "28.25%", "added": false}, {"text": "30.35%", "added": false}, {"text": "25.58%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "The areas of two similar triangles are 48 cm2and 156 cm2. If the height of the smaller triangle is 6 cm, then the corresponding height (in cm) of the bigger triangle is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "congruence-and-similarity", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "If a number P is 15% less than another number Q, and Q is 12% more than 156, then what is the value of P?", "options": [{"text": "168.52", "added": false}, {"text": "138.52", "added": false}, {"text": "148.51", "added": false}, {"text": "178.52", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "The sum of three distinct prime numbers is 44. What is the largest possible prime number?", "options": [{"text": "37", "added": false}, {"text": "31", "added": false}, {"text": "41", "added": false}, {"text": "43", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "types-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "A person got a new chair at 35% discount. Had he got no discount, he would have had to pay ₹224 more. What is the marked price (in ₹) of the chair?", "options": [{"text": "735", "added": false}, {"text": "640", "added": false}, {"text": "600", "added": false}, {"text": "750", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "The price of sugar goes up by 25%. By how much percentage must a family reduce their consumption of sugar so that the expenditure on sugar remains the same?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "The HCF of 0.0006, 0.006, 0.06, 0.6 and 6 is:", "options": [{"text": "0.6", "added": false}, {"text": "0.06", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "0.0006", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-fractions", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "2150", "added": false}, {"text": "2200", "added": false}, {"text": "2175", "added": false}, {"text": "2225", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": null}]}